"""Gate profiles per control point (EVOL-046): no gate is optional — it changes its control point.

mode       ONE key, `delivery_mode` at the top of the governance manifest (`development` | `production`), read by
           ONE definition that fails closed: an absent key, an unknown value or an unreadable manifest is
           `production`; no environment variable overrides it.
profile    derived from the mode and the branch class (gates/branch.py): `light` only for a sub-increment while
           the project is in development mode; `full` for everything else — the train close, a plain branch, a
           malformed or unclassifiable name, and every branch in production mode.
members    the gate members, enumerated by PROPERTY: `light` = the members that need no build and no database;
           `full` = every member. Each member names its owner — the reader runs the script members at the push /
           CI control points (all-report: every member reports, one verdict names every red member and what was
           skipped); agent-run members (the full verification loop, the sweep, the smoke) are owed to their owner
           at their control point and listed as such. The light profile writes no seal.
"""
